  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a positive integer KKK and a sequence A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​. Initially, each element of this sequence is 000 or 111; your goal is to make all elements equal to 000.\n\nIn order to do that, you may perform the following operation any number of times:\n\n\nChoose a subarray (a contiguous subsequence) with length KKK, i.e. choose two indices LLL and RRR such that 1≤L≤R≤N1 \\le L \\le R \\le N1≤L≤R≤N and R−L+1=KR-L+1 = KR−L+1=K.\nChoose one element of that subarray and change it to 000, i.e. choose an index PPP such that L≤P≤RL \\le P \\le RL≤P≤R and change APA_PAP​ to 000.\nThe cost of this operation is the sum of this subarray AL+AL+1+…+ARA_L + A_{L+1} + \\ldots + A_RAL​+AL+1​+…+AR​ before APA_PAP​ is changed.\nFind the minimum total cost (sum of costs of individual operations) of making all elements of AAA equal to 000.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2001 \\le T \\le 2001≤T≤200",
      "1≤K≤N≤2⋅1051 \\le K \\le N \\le 2 \\cdot 10^51≤K≤N≤2⋅105",
      "0≤Ai≤10 \\le A_i \\le 10≤Ai​≤1 for each valid iii",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 4⋅1054 \\cdot 10^54⋅105"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN and KKK.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer ― the minimum cost of turning all elements of AAA into zeros.",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n5 3\n1 0 1 0 1\n4 4\n1 1 0 1\n3 1\n1 1 0",
        "output": "3\n6\n2",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nExample case 1: The minimum cost is 333 and it can be obtained using the following sequence of operations:\n\nchoose the subarray [L,R]=[2,4][L,R] = [2,4][L,R]=[2,4] and set A3=0A_3=0A3​=0 with cost 111\nchoose the subarray [1,3][1,3][1,3] and set A1=0A_1=0A1​=0 with cost 111\nchoose the subarray [3,5][3,5][3,5] and set A5=0A_5=0A5​=0 with cost 111\n\nExample case 2: We have to choose the whole sequence ([L,R]=[1,4][L,R] = [1,4][L,R]=[1,4]) in each operation, so the total cost is 3+2+1=63+2+1=63+2+1=6:\n\nchoose the subarray [1,4][1,4][1,4] and set A1=0A_1=0A1​=0 with cost 333\nchoose the subarray [1,4][1,4][1,4] and set A2=0A_2=0A2​=0 with cost 222\nchoose the subarray [1,4][1,4][1,4] and set A4=0A_4=0A4​=0 with cost 111\n\nExample case 3: The minimum cost is 222 and it can be obtained using the following sequence of operations:\n\nchoose the subarray [2,2][2,2][2,2] and set A2=0A_2=0A2​=0 with cost 111\nchoose the subarray [1,1][1,1][1,1] and set A1=0A_1=0A1​=0 with cost 111"
      }
    ]
  },
